    <item>
      <title>Isabella Weber's Vision for an Affordability Agenda</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-11-27/isabella-weber-s-vision-for-an-affordability-agenda-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">7a4469204bbe19ce1c641949</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:13:04 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The most important word in politics right now is affordability. It was a winning issue in the midterms for Democrats, and one of the reasons why people across Europe are out in the streets protesting: Food, housing, and energy are getting more expensive by the day. During the height of the pandemic, we talked a lot about inflation with Isabella Weber, and her on what governments can do to make life more affordable has evolved into a book called Anti-Fascist Economics: In Defense of Affordability, Dignity, and Democracy. It is part-history, part-manifesto, and it maps out why things got so expensive and what can be done to get prices down. Today, we speak to Weber about why CPI, in her opinion, is a misleading measure, why fridges got cheaper but groceries got pricier, rebuilding state capacity, strategies for price controls, China's strategic pork reserve, and her new book. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
