      <pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:52:57 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Bloomberg Daybreak Europe is your essential morning viewing to stay ahead. Live from Brussels, we set the agenda for your day, catching you up with overnight markets news from the US and Asia. And we'll tell you what matters for investors in Europe, giving you insight before trading begins.

Investors piled back into equities at the end of a holiday-shortened week as the AI trade rebounded and China stepped up support for its stock market.

Leaders meeting in Brussels agreed to recommend Pablo Hernández de Cos as the next ECB President. He will succeed Christine Lagarde, who will end her term early on February 7.

Plus, Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez says Spain risks public spending cuts so deep they’d trigger a recession if the far-right gets into government after Sunday’s election.

Today's guest: Lizzy Galbraith, Aberdeen, Senior Political Economist. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
